we should perhaps not be desperately  surprised with the line taken by mr  peskov in the sense that it is exactly  what vladimir putin has been saying what  their ambassador to the united nations  has been saying when presented with  evidence they simply hold up their hands  and say nothing to do with us  well  it's not true is it and and i think  they're very good at fake news and we  just need to  know that what we're saying is correct  we know we have journalists who are  disciplined and thoughtful and make sure  that they have clear sources and we just  have to carry on telling the truth but  more importantly gathering information  so that when the time comes we can take  out prosecutions against the relevant  people we must hold them to account for  the war crimes that they're obviously  committing and i mean the truth is is  that is that the evidence that we have  at the moment is just the tip of the  iceberg i fear you know because we're  only seeing it from the towns and  villages where the russians have  withdrawn there are many other towns and  villages where the russians are still in  occupation and we just don't know the  full extent of the horror in the in  those areas but just in terms of of  prosecuting war crimes and certainly  people wish to establish what what  actually has taken place in various  parts of the country but but given  russia's relationship or lack of  relationship with the icc how is it  possible you can have a special tribunal  basically that's what you can do and you  know we  where there's a will essentially i mean  remember people couldn't believe that we  would ever be able to hold the murderers  in yugoslavia to account and yet we did  in the end and we got most of the major  players you know stood trial rightly and  are now behind bars rightly  in terms of of what we have seen from  from nato in the past 24 hours there  feels like what there has been a there  has been an escalation nato has agreed  that they will be providing 